Cedrus stateless V4L2 video decoder ("sunxi-cedrus") from the Fedora kernel,
copied under another module name ("a733-cedrus") with one variant: the
Allwinner A733 decoder block on the Radxa Cubie A7A. Compile-tested only;
nothing here has run on the board (TESTING.md).

Packaging: cubie-a7a-vdec (DKMS, every codec built in, chosen per module
parameter), with the patch sets of ../a733-cedrus-hevc-vp8 (0001-0005),
../a733-cedrus-mpeg-h264 (0001-0004), ../a733-cedrus-vp9 (0001; 0002 as
rebased onto the per-codec switches) and ../a733-cedrus-jpeg (0001, rebased;
JPEG capability bit 7) applied here. Builds with W=1 and passes modpost
against 7.3.3-300.fc45.aarch64 with every codec and with none of the
optional ones. Loaded by cubie-a7a-hat.service after sun55i-pck600; the
device tree node is in fedora/dts/cubie-a7a-video-codec.dtsi (binding
stamp 16).

Source:  Fedora kernel-7.3.3-300.fc45.src.rpm
         sha256 7f1a1de7f12d1dd9a1560ad6a9b0a59e0d75698c489671ba2297c1d27f7ca4e8
Tarball: linux-7.3.3.tar.xz
         sha256 dab92554b98f51a00055b96733b9efe35b2011e5a5f64003c48e4c94dd9a1c01
Path:    linux-7.3.3/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus (the thirteen .c/.h
         files; sha256 of the unmodified files in UPSTREAM.sha256). The
         in-tree Kconfig, Makefile and TODO are not copied.
License: GPL-2.0 per file (MODULE_LICENSE "GPL v2"); headers unchanged.

Changes (cedrus.c, cedrus.h, cedrus_hw.c, cedrus_regs.h, cedrus_h264.c,
cedrus_h265.c, cedrus_mpeg2.c and cedrus_vp8.c; the other five files are
the upstream files byte for byte):
  - in-tree Makefile replaced by Makefile (same objects, module
    a733-cedrus.ko; A733_CEDRUS_HEVC=1, A733_CEDRUS_HEVC10=1 and
    A733_CEDRUS_VP8=1 define A733_CEDRUS_CODEC_H265, _H265_10 and _VP8;
    A733_CEDRUS_EXPERIMENTAL=1 sets all three)
  - cedrus.h: CEDRUS_NAME "cedrus" -> "a733-cedrus" (platform driver name,
    video device name, media device model and bus_info, VIDIOC_QUERYCAP
    driver/card), so the in-tree module can be loaded next to this one
  - cedrus.h: CEDRUS_QUIRK_A733; struct cedrus_variant gains quirks; struct
    cedrus_dev gains quirks, ahb_gate_clk, mbus_gate_clk, syscfg
  - cedrus.c: the eleven in-tree variants and match entries removed; one
    variant and match entry added, "allwinner,sun60i-a733-video-engine":
    untiled output, MPEG-2, H.264, module clock 624 MHz; H.265, H.265
    10-bit and VP8 each only with its A733_CEDRUS_CODEC_* define
  - cedrus.c: MODULE_DESCRIPTION names the copy
  - cedrus_hw.c: sunxi_sram_claim()/sunxi_sram_release() and the
    sunxi_sram.h include removed (Fedora's built-in sunxi_sram has no A733
    system-control entry, so the claim could only fail). In their place,
    for CEDRUS_QUIRK_A733: the node's second reg entry (system control,
    mapped without requesting it) and, on every runtime resume, bit 0 of
    +0x0 and bit 24 of +0x4 cleared
  - cedrus_hw.c: for CEDRUS_QUIRK_A733 a 32-bit DMA mask is set, and the
    optional clocks "ahb-gate" and "mbus-gate" are taken and enabled before
    / disabled after the three in-tree clocks
  - cedrus_hw.c: for CEDRUS_QUIRK_A733 bits 0 and 4 of VE register 0x804
    are set and cleared again after the clocks come up and after the
    watchdog's reset
  - cedrus_regs.h, cedrus.h, cedrus_hw.c: for CEDRUS_QUIRK_A733 the version
    registers 0xf0, 0xe0 and 0xe4 are read once at the first runtime resume
    and printed; the decoder IP version is kept in struct cedrus_dev
  - cedrus_h265.c: bit 31 of the control register is set with the interrupt
    enables when the decoder IP version is 0x31010, 0x33010, 0x33210,
    0x33310, 0x33321 or 0x30520
  - cedrus.h, cedrus_vp8.c: deblocking and intra prediction line buffers
    for coded widths above 2048 and the buffer control register written at
    every setup; a frame header larger than the coded format is refused;
    the entropy probability buffer is 0x5400 bytes instead of 0x2400
  - cedrus_h264.c, cedrus_mpeg2.c: an H.264 SPS or MPEG-2 sequence that
    needs more macroblocks than the coded format is refused
  - cedrus_h264.c: deblocking line buffer at least (columns + 31) * 192
    bytes, motion vector field halves at least the vendor's size, 16 KiB
    picture-info slots from 2048 pixels wide
  - cedrus_regs.h, cedrus_h264.c: for CEDRUS_QUIRK_A733 bit 10 of the
    H.264 control register (0x220) is written at the start of every frame
    and kept with the interrupt enables
  - cedrus.h, cedrus_hw.c: the encoder IP version is kept as well; bit 10
    of the mode register is set for the decoder/encoder IP version pairs
    0x33310/0x21320, 0x33210/0x12011 and 0x33321/0x21321

Optional JPEG decoder (A733_CEDRUS_JPEG=1 in Makefile adds cedrus_jpeg.o
and defines A733_CEDRUS_JPEG):
  - cedrus_jpeg.c, cedrus_jpeg_regs.h: new files, not from the Fedora
    tarball. A second video node "a733-cedrus-jpeg" (JPEG in, NV12 out)
    that decodes baseline JPEG with the MPEG engine and shares this
    module's m2m device, interrupt handler and watchdog. Register
    programming after the public cedrus JPEG series by Emmanuel Gil Peyrot
    and Jernej Skrabec (linux-media, 2024-07-31, Message-ID
    20240731164422.206503-1-linkmauve@linkmauve.fr, GPL-2.0, not merged)
  - cedrus.h: CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_JPEG_DEC (bit 7 here: the VP9 decoder
    holds bit 6, which the JPEG series used), struct cedrus_ctx
    codec.jpeg, struct cedrus_dev vfd_jpeg, and the register/unregister
    hooks (inline no-ops without A733_CEDRUS_JPEG)
  - cedrus.c: the hooks called at the end of probe (failure only warns)
    and at the start of remove; the A733 variant gains
    CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_JPEG_DEC under A733_CEDRUS_JPEG
  - cedrus_hw.c: cedrus_engine_enable() selects the MPEG engine for
    V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG
  - needs v4l2-jpeg.ko (CONFIG_V4L2_JPEG_HELPER=m in Fedora's aarch64
    configuration, shipped in kernel-modules)

Sources read for the A733 values include:
  - vendor kernel driver, https://github.com/alexcaoys/allwinner-bsp branch
    linux-6.18.y, commit 656a550c826787e7e72fae58ca793df9e0988ac8,
    drivers/ve/cedar-ve/cedar_ve.c: set_sys_cfg_by_self() (the two
    system-control bits), set_vcu_en_regmode_to1_to0() (register 0x804),
    enable_cedar_hw_clk_module() (clock set and order), and
    platforms/ve_plat_common.c: ve_irq_work() (mode select at +0x0; MPEG at
    0x100, H.264 at 0x200, HEVC at 0x500, as in cedrus_regs.h)
  - vendor device tree and CCU, the same repository and commit:
    configs/linux-6.6/sun60iw2p1.dtsi (ve@1c0e000),
    sun60iw2p1-cpu-vf.dtsi (624 MHz at 800 mV for every speed bin),
    drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60iw2.c
  - sunxi_sram.c of the same Fedora tarball: the H616 "VE" section is reg
    0x0 bit 0 and the A64 "C" section reg 0x4 bit 24, both 1 = CPU and
    0 = device, the same two bits the vendor driver clears
  - libvdpau-sunxi, https://github.com/linux-sunxi/libvdpau-sunxi commit
    ebdf7844efbb997a1e858600ae76c90985ea865d (LGPL-2.1+), h264.c: the same
    control bit 10 and line buffer sizes; read for comparison, no code
    taken
  - the variant's capability list and rate were first proposed in
    https://github.com/jonas5/Allwinner-A733-kernel,
    patch/0003-allwinner-a733-cedrus-vpu-support.patch (a hint; that patch
    carries no SRAM, clock or reset handling)
